WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.520
Fast X's surprise cameo has left audiences&nbsp;
rocked. Does this herald a new direction for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:08.820
the franchise's end? Or does it mark&nbsp;
a return to the Fast Family's roots?

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.080
Spoilers ahead!

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:15.480
The off-screen rivalry between Vin Diesel and&nbsp;
Dwayne Johnson is no secret. After starring in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:19.440
three franchise installments together, Johnson&nbsp;
returned once more for the eighth feature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:23.400
"The Fate of the Furious." Following the&nbsp;
film's release, both Johnson and Diesel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.840
alluded to some serious on-set tension that&nbsp;
continued to bubble into the production of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:31.320
the next installments. But, instead of&nbsp;
continuing to star opposite one another,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:35.160
Johnson was given the reins to the first&nbsp;
and only "Fast &amp; Furious" spin-off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:40.020
"Hobbs &amp; Shaw," where he starred opposite&nbsp;
Jason Statham. Diesel continued on with "F9,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:44.520
which neglected to even mention Hobbs, though&nbsp;
Statham's Shaw appeared in a mid-credits scene.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:48.660
Despite the high tensions between these&nbsp;
two mega-stars, Johnson returns to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:53.100
franchise in a post-credits cameo for&nbsp;
"Fast X." After 2019's "Hobbs &amp; Shaw,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.100
and Johnson's previous comments about&nbsp;
not returning to the "Fast" family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:00.180
many thought the character was gone for good.&nbsp;
Things seemed especially dire when Johnson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:05.280
ignored Diesel's social media peace offering&nbsp;
where he asked the former WWE superstar to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.880
return to the franchise for the sake of the&nbsp;
fans. With Hobbs' return, maybe the feud&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:13.440
between Johnson and Diesel is finally over. Due&nbsp;
to their past, it's unlikely that Johnson would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:18.900
work with Diesel again if things off-screen hadn't&nbsp;
changed, giving us hope for "Fast &amp; Furious 11."

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:23.400
With "Fast &amp; Furious Presents: Hobbs &amp; Shaw,"&nbsp;
Johnson and Statham showed their characters'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:28.440
potential to headline a major motion picture&nbsp;
without Diesel's Dom Toretto and family. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:32.640
the film expanded on the "Fast &amp; Furious"&nbsp;
universe, introducing the techno-terrorist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:38.280
organization Eteon, the superhuman Brixton Lore,&nbsp;
and the extended families of both titular action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:42.420
heroes. While these additions might not seem like&nbsp;
much outside of the context of "Hobbs &amp; Shaw,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:46.560
there's a possibility that they may have some&nbsp;
serious ramifications on the franchise at large,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:50.280
especially as Johnson and Statham&nbsp;
return to mainline "The Fast Saga."

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:55.140
Since the introduction of Kurt Russell's Mr.&nbsp;
Nobody in "Furious 7," the franchise has shifted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:59.760
from street races and extensive car heists&nbsp;
to global espionage and world-ending threats.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:04.560
"Hobbs &amp; Shaw" was no different, revealing that&nbsp;
Eteon is in control of many of the world's media&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:09.600
outlets, with goals of global domination. Since&nbsp;
Hobbs left the Toretto crew to continue enforcing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:14.100
law and order elsewhere, bringing some of that&nbsp;
back with him isn't out of the question. Though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:17.940
Eteon hasn't shown up in "The Fast Saga" yet,&nbsp;
the return of Hobbs could reveal that he's on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:22.140
the criminal organization's tail, especially&nbsp;
after the mysterious Director's threats.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:26.820
"You don't remember me, do you, Hobbs? You will."

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:31.440
Likewise, the introduction of Hobbs' extended&nbsp;
family of warriors in his spin-off feature may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:35.820
end up factoring into the 11th installment&nbsp;
somehow. After all, this franchise is about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:40.320
family. That said, it might be a bit jarring for&nbsp;
the events of a spinoff film to factor into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:44.820
swan song of a franchise 10 mainline movies&nbsp;
deep, so we'll just have to wait and see.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:49.620
Speaking of "Hobbs &amp; Shaw," initial sequel&nbsp;
talks were had following the release of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:53.940
"Fast &amp; Furious" spin-off, but we haven't heard&nbsp;
much about a continuation since. Though Johnson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:57.840
seemed confident that another installment&nbsp;
would be made, it seems as if the folks at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:01.980
Universal Pictures have been hyper-focused&nbsp;
on closing out "The Fast Saga" first. With&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:07.740
2021's "F9" and 2023's "Fast X" both coming&nbsp;
out since Johnson and Statham's buddy flick,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:12.180
it's clear that the studio's priorities&nbsp;
lie elsewhere, at least for now. In 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:15.960
producer Kelly McCormick confirmed to&nbsp;
comicbook.com that though they'd love to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:20.040
make another "Hobbs &amp; Shaw" in the future, there&nbsp;
are, quote, "no conversations at this time."

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:24.540
But that was then, and this is now. With&nbsp;
Johnson's return for "Fast X," and likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:28.980
the eleventh "Fast Saga" film as well, maybe this&nbsp;
is The Rock's way of reigniting interest in his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:32.880
character after a few years of silence.&nbsp;
No doubt, after the box-office bomb that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:36.120
was "Black Adam," Johnson's venture&nbsp;
into the DC Comics superhero space,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:41.040
the mega-star is likely attempting to revisit&nbsp;
his known successes. Since his time as Luke Hobbs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:44.940
has always led to high box office returns,&nbsp;
coming back to "The Fast Saga" seems like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:48.960
the right move after failing to restructure&nbsp;
the hierarchy of power in the DC Universe.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:53.640
Since Johnson's departure following "The Fate&nbsp;
of the Furious," the series has brought along&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:59.040
another WWE champion into their ranks. In "F9,"&nbsp;
John Cena serves as the primary antagonist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:02.520
playing Dom Toretto's long-lost brother&nbsp;
Jakob. Over the course of the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:06.480
Dom and Jakob make amends, leading to the&nbsp;
latter's return for "Fast X," in which he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:10.620
helps save his nephew from Dom's latest&nbsp;
antagonist, Dante Reyes. Though Jakob&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:14.580
seemingly gives his life for his family, it's&nbsp;
hard to say what the future holds—after all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:18.300
even death can't stop characters from returning&nbsp;
to the Toretto family again and again.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:23.640
All that is to say, Jakob and Hobbs, played by&nbsp;
two WWE legends, may finally meet in the "Fast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:28.140
and Furious" franchise. With the way "Fast X"&nbsp;
honors previous franchise installments and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:32.400
occasionally non-linear nature of "The Fast Saga"&nbsp;
as a whole, it's entirely possible that Luke Hobbs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:36.480
and Jakob Toretto could have met sometime in&nbsp;
the not-too-distant past. Or maybe even the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:41.700
"Fast &amp; Furious" franchise isn't big enough for&nbsp;
two WWE heroes to coexist in it at the same time.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:47.580
In its fourth outing, 2009's "Fast &amp; Furious," the&nbsp;
series returned to its street racing and criminal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:52.200
roots, reuniting Vin Diesel's Dom and Paul&nbsp;
Walker's Brian for a brand new adventure. Then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:56.340
when 2011's "Fast Five" was released, the&nbsp;
franchise was reborn through a series of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.340 --> 00:05:00.000
extensive heists and new cast members who&nbsp;
helped rebuild the series into something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.140
bigger and better. Dwayne Johnson was one&nbsp;
of those cast members, and his character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:08.400
Luke Hobbs introduced new opportunities to the&nbsp;
Toretto crew that kept them racing for years.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:12.720
In fact, Hobbs is the guy to take out&nbsp;
"Fast Five" antagonist Hernan Reyes. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:17.220
bringing the Rock back for "Fast X" — itself a&nbsp;
direct continuation of "Fast Five" — only makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:21.300
sense. As Jason Momoa's Dante Reyes plans&nbsp;
to destroy those who killed his father,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:24.000
"Fast X" reveals that Hobbs likewise is a target.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:28.800
However the 11th installment shapes up, the events&nbsp;
of "Fast Five" — considered one of the best in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:33.000
franchise — are still propelling the overall&nbsp;
series plot forward. By bringing Hobbs back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:36.540
it shows that the filmmakers behind the&nbsp;
multi-part finale are hoping to honor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:39.780
the franchise to its core, giving each&nbsp;
and every character their due diligence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:44.100
Here's hoping that more familiar faces&nbsp;
will return for "Fast &amp; Furious 11."

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:48.420
For years, the name Dwayne Johnson has brought&nbsp;
in the big bucks. Between his chiseled features&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:53.340
and intense charisma, the former WWE star&nbsp;
certainly knows how to entertain a diverse crowd.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:58.020
Having ventured into comedies, action films,&nbsp;
superhero productions, and animated features,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:01.800
there are very few genres that The Rock&nbsp;
hasn't attempted to break into. Sure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:06.600
he's had some bombs along the way, but generally&nbsp;
speaking, franchises like "Fast &amp; Furious" and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:10.440
"Jumanji" have been massive hits for the&nbsp;
wrestler-turned-movie star. To this day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:13.500
"Furious 7" is still the actor's&nbsp;
highest-grossing picture, having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:18.660
brought in $1.5 billion worldwide. No wonder&nbsp;
he'd eventually make a furious comeback with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:22.320
the series that's brought him the most success.&nbsp;
We're just surprised he didn't do it faster.

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:23.940
"Daddy's gotta go to work."

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:28.020
Needless to say, Johnson's four "Fast&nbsp;
Saga" installments and his "Hobbs &amp; Shaw"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:33.240
solo venture have done tremendously well, bringing&nbsp;
in new audiences along the way. With Johnson's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:36.720
return to the franchise, plus the additional&nbsp;
novelty of these films being the beginning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:40.980
of the end for the series as we know it, the&nbsp;
likelihood of high box office returns is high.

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:45.600
Recent "Fast &amp; Furious" installments have made&nbsp;
it a point to highlight the children of the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:49.680
popular characters in the series. In "Fate of&nbsp;
the Furious," Dom was introduced to his son with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:54.780
Elena, who he later named Brian. Similarly, "Hobbs&nbsp;
&amp; Shaw" highlights Hobbs' daughter Sam, and Brian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:58.620
and Mia's children are mentioned on more than&nbsp;
one occasion throughout the last few films. Yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:03.540
found family is the bedrock of "The Fast Saga,"&nbsp;
but the next generation matters too. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:08.340
the non-canon animated series "Fast &amp; Furious:&nbsp;
Spy Racers" is all about a younger generation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:12.600
of operatives led by Dom's cousin Tony&nbsp;
as they use fast cars to save the world.

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:16.800
By bringing Hobbs back into the fold, and&nbsp;
giving "Fast X" an emphasis on fathers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:20.880
and their children, Johnson's return might&nbsp;
mark a new era for "The Fast Saga." While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:24.120
the story of Dom's crew may end soon,&nbsp;
that doesn't mean the "Fast &amp; Furious"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:27.900
franchise will officially fade to black.&nbsp;
Instead, it's possible that a new series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:30.660
featuring the Toretto gang's kids&nbsp;
may be developed in the future.

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:35.760
Since the end of "Fast Five," this franchise has&nbsp;
made it clear that death isn't the end for many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:39.840
of our recurring heroes. From Letty's survival&nbsp;
after her apparent murder in the fourth film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:43.320
to Han surviving his explosive end&nbsp;
in "Tokyo Drift," there's no telling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:47.040
who could come back in the future. Even&nbsp;
characters like Sean Boswell from "Tokyo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:51.300
Drift," who made his return via a cameo in&nbsp;
"Furious 7" before officially reappearing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:55.080
in "F9," find themselves reuniting with Dom&nbsp;
and his crew at some point down the line.

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:58.620
With that in mind, Johnson's return&nbsp;
as Hobbs, as unlikely as it seemed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:03.120
isn't exactly surprising. After "Fast X,"&nbsp;
it's a wonder who else might return in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:07.680
future. The final chapters of "The Fast Saga"&nbsp;
shouldn't be overstuffed, but Hobbs reentering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:11.040
the Family means the door is open for other&nbsp;
characters to get back behind the wheel.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:15.840
In the past, Dwayne Johnson has received top&nbsp;
billing for his "Fast &amp; Furious" appearances&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:20.580
alongside Vin Diesel and Paul Walker. Though the&nbsp;
latter two are clearly the stars of the franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:24.960
Johnson has doggedly attempted to carve out a&nbsp;
clear slice of the "Fast Saga" pie for himself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:29.580
No doubt, this led to the initial feud between&nbsp;
Johnson and Diesel, but now that the hatchet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:33.840
seems to be buried, there may be hope for fans&nbsp;
who want to see more of Hobbs. While Johnson's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:37.860
return could very well lead to more "Hobbs &amp;&nbsp;
Shaw" movies going forward, it's not necessarily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:42.060
impossible that Hobbs Johnson could take center&nbsp;
stage in future "Fast &amp; Furious" movies."

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:45.720
Since Hobbs already tried that during "The&nbsp;
Fate of the Furious," it wouldn't be a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:50.040
surprise to see him leading the group going&nbsp;
forward. Obviously, no one can replace Dom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:53.640
but that doesn't mean that the "Fast &amp;&nbsp;
Furious" brand couldn't live on without him.

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:55.080
"I'm always here."

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:59.940
Diesel didn't appear at all in Paul Walker's&nbsp;
sequel, "2 Fast 2 Furious," and he only had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.940 --> 00:09:04.560
a small cameo in "Tokyo Drift." Admittedly,&nbsp;
there hasn't been a second mainline "Fast Saga"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:08.940
movie yet that doesn't feature Diesel in some&nbsp;
capacity, but it's at least a possibility that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:13.080
Johnson could carry the "Fast &amp; Furious"&nbsp;
torch once Dom's story is finally done.

